# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Format: CVE-ID or vulnerability ID, one per line
# Add comments with # to explain why each vulnerability is ignored

# ===================================================================
# cos-nodejs-sdk-v5 依赖了已废弃的 `request` 库，其间接依赖
# (form-data, qs) 存在漏洞。已通过 pnpm overrides 修复。
# 如果 Trivy 仍然通过 lock 文件检测到旧版本，可忽略以下 CVE。
# ===================================================================

# form-data unsafe random boundary (cos-nodejs-sdk-v5 > request > form-data)
# 已通过 pnpm overrides 强制升级到 >=4.0.0
GHSA-fjxv-7rqg-78g4

# qs arrayLimit bypass DoS (cos-nodejs-sdk-v5 > request > qs)
# 已通过 pnpm overrides 强制升级到 >=6.14.1
GHSA-6rw7-vpxm-498p

# minimatch ReDoS (CVE-2026-26996) — affects 3.1.2, 5.1.6, 9.0.5
# These are dev-only transitive deps (test-exclude, eslint, glob).
# Cannot upgrade to ESM-only 10.x without breaking Jest coverage (CJS).
# Production minimatch@10.x already patched via pnpm override.
CVE-2026-26996

# ===================================================================
# Docker image transitive dependency CVEs
# These are dev/build-time dependencies in the container image,
# not exploitable in production runtime.
# ===================================================================

# cross-spawn ReDoS — dev-only (used by npm/eslint toolchain)
CVE-2024-21538

# glob prototype pollution — dev-only transitive dep
CVE-2025-64756

# minimatch ReDoS (additional CVEs beyond CVE-2026-26996)
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# zlib memory corruption — Node.js built-in, mitigated by container isolation
CVE-2026-22184

# ===================================================================
# REMOVED: the node-tar 6.2.1 block and sigstore CVE-2026-48815.
#
# Both were attributed to `pnpm deploy --prod` resolving old versions "despite
# pnpm.overrides". That was wrong, and the wrong attribution is what made these
# entries keep growing new CVE ids: tar 6.2.1, brace-expansion 2.0.1 and
# sigstore 2.3.1 were never in our lockfile at all. They lived in the base
# image's own bundled npm, under usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/. No override
# could ever have reached them.
#
# apps/api/Dockerfile now upgrades that npm to 11, which brings tar 7.x,
# a patched brace-expansion and sigstore 4.x, so these findings are gone rather
# than silenced. If a future Trivy finding names a package at a version the
# lockfile does not contain, check `usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/` and any
# dependency's `dist/compiled/` before adding an entry here.
# ===================================================================

# ===================================================================
# brace-expansion CVE-2026-14257 (HIGH, = GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg) — DoS via
# unbounded brace expansion, affects 1.1.16 and 2.1.2. No patched release
# exists on either line; the fix ships only in 5.0.8. Forcing everything to
# >=5.0.8 resolves cleanly and then breaks the toolchain (5.x drops the
# callable CJS default export, so minimatch@3.1.5 under eslint 9 throws
# "expand is not a function" and all three lint:* scripts die). 1.x/2.x reach
# us only via minimatch@3/@9, whose patterns come from our own configs and
# never from user input, so the DoS is not reachable.
#
# This is the SAME exemption as pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas, documented in
# docs/SECURITY_DEPS.md. Both gates scan the lockfile and both report it, so
# an exemption has to be recorded in BOTH places or one gate stays red.
# Remove from here and from ignoreGhsas together.
# ===================================================================
CVE-2026-14257
